DETAILED ANALYSIS
======================================================================

1. EMT Performance:
   • C-C Bond Length:  1.0096 Å  (error: 34.27%)
   • C-C Bond Energy:  2.1591 eV (error: 43.33%)
   • EMT severely underestimates the C-C bond length and bond energy
   • This is expected - EMT is a simple effective medium theory

2. MACE Performance:
   • C-C Bond Length:  1.5218 Å  (error: 0.92%)
   • C-C Bond Energy:  3.7342 eV (error: 1.99%)
   • MACE gives much better agreement with experiment
   • The bond length is particularly accurate

3. Method Comparison:
   ✓ MACE gives better bond length (0.0142 Å vs 0.5264 Å)
   ✓ MACE gives better bond energy (0.0758 eV vs 1.6509 eV)

4. Key Insights:
   • EMT underestimates the C-C bond length by 0.5264 Å
     This is because EMT treats the molecule as an electron gas,
     leading to over-binding and artificially short bonds.

   • EMT underestimates the C-C bond energy by 1.6509 eV
     The bond is too weak in EMT because the potential is too soft.

   • MACE, being trained on accurate DFT data, captures the
     correct PES curvature and gives much better results.

5. Why MACE is better for this system:
   • Ethane is an organic molecule with covalent bonds
   • EMT was designed for metals and simple systems
   • MACE was trained on diverse molecular datasets including organics
   • The machine-learned potential captures many-body effects
   • MACE can describe the subtle electronic structure of C-C bonds

